{"id":"bgw2pw","title":"bgw2pw.x","program":"bgw2pw.x","package":"PWscf","version":"7.5","html":"<section class=\"qe-section qe-sec-intro\" id=\"intro\" data-kind=\"intro\" data-title=\"Introduction\"><h2 class=\"qe-section-title\">Introduction</h2>\n\n<div class=\"qe-indent\"><pre class=\"qe-pre\"><b>Purpose of bgw2pw.x:</b>\n   Converts BerkeleyGW WFN and RHO files to the format of pw.x.\n   NO LONGER WORKING AFTER v.6.3.\n   This can be useful, for example, if you generate the plane waves\n   on top of the valence bands and want to diagonalize them in pw.x.\n   Look at the documentation for SAPO code in BerkeleyGW for more information.</pre>\n<p class=\"qe-flow\">bgw2pw.x reads common parameters from file <a href=\"#prefix\" data-local=\"prefix\">prefix</a>.save/data-file.xml and\nwrites files <a href=\"#prefix\" data-local=\"prefix\">prefix</a>.save/charge-density.dat (charge density in R-space),\n<a href=\"#prefix\" data-local=\"prefix\">prefix</a>.save/gvectors.dat (G-vectors for charge density and potential),\n<a href=\"#prefix\" data-local=\"prefix\">prefix</a>.save/K$n/eigenval.xml (eigenvalues and occupations for nth k-point),\n<a href=\"#prefix\" data-local=\"prefix\">prefix</a>.save/K$n/evc.dat (wavefunctions in G-space for nth k-point), and\n<a href=\"#prefix\" data-local=\"prefix\">prefix</a>.save/K$n/gkvectors.dat (G-vectors for nth k-point).</p>\n<p class=\"qe-flow\">bgw2pw.x doesn't modify file <a href=\"#prefix\" data-local=\"prefix\">prefix</a>.save/data-file.xml so make changes to this\nfile manually (for example, you will need to change the number of bands if you\nare using bgw2pw.x in conjunction with SAPO code in BerkeleyGW).</p>\n<pre class=\"qe-pre\"><b>Structure of the input data:</b>\n============================\n\n<b>&amp;INPUT_BGW2PW</b>\n  ...\n<b>/</b></pre></div>\n</section>\n   <section class=\"qe-section qe-sec-namelist\" id=\"INPUT_BGW2PW\" data-kind=\"namelist\" data-title=\"&amp;INPUT_BGW2PW\" data-name=\"INPUT_BGW2PW\"><h2 class=\"qe-section-title\"><span class=\"qe-kind\">Namelist</span> <span class=\"qe-nl\">&amp;INPUT_BGW2PW</span></h2><div class=\"qe-layout\">\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"prefix\" data-var=\"prefix\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#prefix\">prefix</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">STRING</span> <span class=\"qe-status\">MANDATORY</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"prefix\"></span></header><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">prefix of files saved by program pw.x</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"outdir\" data-var=\"outdir\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#outdir\">outdir</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">STRING</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"outdir\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>'./'</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">the scratch directory where the massive data-files are written</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"real_or_complex\" data-var=\"real_or_complex\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#real_or_complex\">real_or_complex</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">INTEGER</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"real_or_complex\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>2</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">1 | 2\n<b>1</b> for real flavor of BerkeleyGW (for systems with inversion symmetry and\ntime-reversal symmetry) or <b>2</b> for complex flavor of BerkeleyGW (for systems\nwithout inversion symmetry and time-reversal symmetry)</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"wfng_flag\" data-var=\"wfng_flag\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#wfng_flag\">wfng_flag</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">LOGICAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"wfng_flag\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>.FALSE.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">read wavefunctions in G-space from BerkeleyGW WFN file</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"wfng_file\" data-var=\"wfng_file\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#wfng_file\">wfng_file</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">STRING</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"wfng_file\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>'WFN'</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">name of BerkeleyGW WFN input file. Not used if <a href=\"#wfng_flag\" data-local=\"wfng_flag\">wfng_flag</a> = .FALSE.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"wfng_nband\" data-var=\"wfng_nband\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#wfng_nband\">wfng_nband</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">INTEGER</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"wfng_nband\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>0</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">number of bands to write (0 = all). Not used if <a href=\"#wfng_flag\" data-local=\"wfng_flag\">wfng_flag</a> = .FALSE.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"rhog_flag\" data-var=\"rhog_flag\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#rhog_flag\">rhog_flag</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">LOGICAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"rhog_flag\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>.FALSE.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">read charge density in G-space from BerkeleyGW RHO file</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"rhog_file\" data-var=\"rhog_file\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#rhog_file\">rhog_file</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">STRING</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"rhog_file\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>'RHO'</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">name of BerkeleyGW RHO input file. Not used if <a href=\"#rhog_flag\" data-local=\"rhog_flag\">rhog_flag</a> = .FALSE.</p></div></article>\n\n   </div></section>","sections":[{"id":"intro","title":"Introduction","kind":"intro","level":0,"varIds":[]},{"id":"INPUT_BGW2PW","title":"&INPUT_BGW2PW","kind":"namelist","name":"INPUT_BGW2PW","level":0,"varIds":["prefix","outdir","real_or_complex","wfng_flag","wfng_file","wfng_nband","rhog_flag","rhog_file"]}],"variables":[{"id":"prefix","names":["prefix"],"display":"prefix","type":"STRING","status":"MANDATORY","sectionId":"INPUT_BGW2PW","sectionTitle":"&INPUT_BGW2PW","options":[],"summary":"prefix of files saved by program pw.x"},{"id":"outdir","names":["outdir"],"display":"outdir","type":"STRING","default":"'./'","sectionId":"INPUT_BGW2PW","sectionTitle":"&INPUT_BGW2PW","options":[],"summary":"the scratch directory where the massive data-files are written"},{"id":"real_or_complex","names":["real_or_complex"],"display":"real_or_complex","type":"INTEGER","default":"2","sectionId":"INPUT_BGW2PW","sectionTitle":"&INPUT_BGW2PW","options":[],"summary":"1 | 2 1 for real flavor of BerkeleyGW (for systems with inversion symmetry and time-reversal symmetry) or 2 for complex flavor of BerkeleyGW (for systems without inversion symmetry and time-reversal symmetry)"},{"id":"wfng_flag","names":["wfng_flag"],"display":"wfng_flag","type":"LOGICAL","default":".FALSE.","sectionId":"INPUT_BGW2PW","sectionTitle":"&INPUT_BGW2PW","options":[],"summary":"read wavefunctions in G-space from BerkeleyGW WFN file"},{"id":"wfng_file","names":["wfng_file"],"display":"wfng_file","type":"STRING","default":"'WFN'","sectionId":"INPUT_BGW2PW","sectionTitle":"&INPUT_BGW2PW","options":[],"summary":"name of BerkeleyGW WFN input file."},{"id":"wfng_nband","names":["wfng_nband"],"display":"wfng_nband","type":"INTEGER","default":"0","sectionId":"INPUT_BGW2PW","sectionTitle":"&INPUT_BGW2PW","options":[],"summary":"number of bands to write (0 = all)."},{"id":"rhog_flag","names":["rhog_flag"],"display":"rhog_flag","type":"LOGICAL","default":".FALSE.","sectionId":"INPUT_BGW2PW","sectionTitle":"&INPUT_BGW2PW","options":[],"summary":"read charge density in G-space from BerkeleyGW RHO file"},{"id":"rhog_file","names":["rhog_file"],"display":"rhog_file","type":"STRING","default":"'RHO'","sectionId":"INPUT_BGW2PW","sectionTitle":"&INPUT_BGW2PW","options":[],"summary":"name of BerkeleyGW RHO input file."}],"aliases":{"id3":"prefix","prefix":"prefix","id4":"outdir","outdir":"outdir","id5":"real_or_complex","real_or_complex":"real_or_complex","id6":"wfng_flag","wfng_flag":"wfng_flag","id7":"wfng_file","wfng_file":"wfng_file","id8":"wfng_nband","wfng_nband":"wfng_nband","id9":"rhog_flag","rhog_flag":"rhog_flag","id10":"rhog_file","rhog_file":"rhog_file","id2":"INPUT_BGW2PW","INPUT_BGW2PW":"INPUT_BGW2PW","id1":"intro"}}